course: dictionary
lesson: 11349
title: Zinc, the metal that guards iron
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Zinc is a bluish-white metal. The dictionary tells you it is a chemical element, which means a pure substance that cannot be broken into anything simpler. Its symbol is Zn.
explain: Context clues show you what zinc does. «Galvanised steel is coated with zinc.» Coated means covered with a thin layer, so zinc is the layer that covers the steel. Read on: «the zinc reacts first and "sacrifices" itself, so the iron stays safe.» The zinc is used up to protect the iron underneath.
explain: Here is a check you can use. Swap a word for its meaning and read the sentence again. «Paint stops rust until it is scratched.» Paint can be damaged, but «galvanised steel has a zinc coat that protects the iron even at a scratch.» Zinc keeps working when paint would fail.
explain: Zinc is also a mineral your body needs. The clue is «in small amounts»: you need only a little, and foods like meat, nuts and beans give it to you. A dictionary entry with numbered meanings, like this one, shows that one word can have more than one sense, so check which sense the sentence uses.
fact: Zinc is a bluish-white metal and a chemical element with the symbol Zn.
fact: «Zinc» is used to coat iron and steel to stop rust.
fact: Galvanised steel has a zinc coat, so the iron stays protected even at a small scratch.
fact: Zinc is a mineral your body needs in small amounts, found in meat, nuts and beans.
fact: Zinc is an uncountable noun, so we say some zinc, not zincs.
exercise: «Galvanised steel is coated with zinc.» What is the zinc doing here? | Turning the steel into food | Painting pictures on the steel | *Covering steel to protect it from rust | Making a coat that protects steel from rust
exercise: Zinc is a chemical element. What does element mean here? | *A pure substance that cannot be broken into simpler substances | A bucket for the garden | A type of sun cream
exercise: Which food is a good source of zinc, the mineral your body needs? | Chocolate buttons | Crisps | *Beans | Fizzy pop
test: «Galvanised steel has a zinc coat that protects the iron even at a scratch.» What does the zinc protect? | *The iron | Paint | The scratch | The ship
test: What colour is zinc? | Bright red | *Bluish-white | Black | Golden yellow
exam: What is the chemical symbol for zinc? | Ze | *Zn | Zc | Zi
